WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.240
A gene is needed for hearing, and its protein sits in the right place.

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:09.560
Is that enough to call it the channel?

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.500
Start with the current.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:16.800
A hair bundle is a staircase of stereocilia, in rows that rise in height.

5
00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:22.403
Tip links connect the tip of each shorter stereocilium to the side of its taller

6
00:00:22.403 --> 00:00:23.403
neighbour.

7
00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.947
Deflect the bundle toward its tallest row.

8
00:00:26.787 --> 00:00:30.127
The tip links are thought to pull channels open near their lower ends.

9
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.860
With the cell held at a negative voltage, cations flow in, and the current is

10
00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:39.500
inward. This is the conventional transduction current.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:43.777
The current rises within a fraction of a millisecond.

12
00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:46.717
That is too fast for a chain of second messengers.

13
00:00:47.517 --> 00:00:49.757
So force is thought to open the channel directly.

14
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.300
Plot the size of the peak current against bundle displacement.

15
00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.520
The S-shaped curve saturates when nearly all channels are open.

16
00:00:59.533 --> 00:01:01.373
That current comes from many channels.

17
00:01:02.353 --> 00:01:03.353
Three things set it.

18
00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:06.967
First, how many working channels sit at the tip links.

19
00:01:07.847 --> 00:01:08.847
Call that N.

20
00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.450
Second, how much current one open channel passes.

21
00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:15.410
That is the unitary current, small i.

22
00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.680
Third, the chance that each channel is open.

23
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.680
That is the open probability, P_open.

24
00:01:22.733 --> 00:01:25.413
For channels that are alike, multiply the three.

25
00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:28.413
That gives the average current from the whole bundle.

26
00:01:29.433 --> 00:01:33.153
Predict. A mutation halves that average current.

27
00:01:34.073 --> 00:01:35.673
Which of the three factors did it change?

28
00:01:41.716 --> 00:01:43.896
From the average alone, you cannot tell.

29
00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:48.116
Halve the channels, the unitary current, or the open probability.

30
00:01:49.216 --> 00:01:50.796
Each gives the same average current.

31
00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:56.560
A trafficking factor, an anchor or a lipid-modifying enzyme could all be needed.

32
00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:59.140
Deleting any one would silence the cell.

33
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.980
So a lost current cannot tell you which factor you removed.

34
00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:07.453
Evidence about permeation speaks more directly to the pore.

35
00:02:08.113 --> 00:02:11.653
Which ions pass, and how much current does one open channel carry?

36
00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:17.236
So do a residue reached in a working channel, and activity of the protein on its

37
00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:20.376
own. But partners can change permeation too.

38
00:02:21.156 --> 00:02:23.376
So the case rests on several rungs together.

39
00:02:24.449 --> 00:02:26.929
Carry one question through every experiment.

40
00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.149
Which factor did it test, and what did it rule out?
